Task: After configuring the manifest delivery controls (carrier route, priority band, delivery window and manifest ID), selecting the integrity binding mode, clicking Snapshot manifest and then submitting Issue seal, the page prints an object to the browser console under action media.sign. Locate the anchor function for the req_sig field of that object. The anchor is the first target-specific signature-token construction function on the dynamic behavior chain: it sits after form-submit coordination, manifest snapshot gating, route-field collection, asynchronous hand-off, factory binding and the per-stage folds, and its own body composes and constructs the target observable request signature token value - rather than merely collecting inputs, dispatching control, packaging a return value, or emitting it to the console sink. Return exactly one complete function together with its code location; do not return a generic utility, an event handler, the whole call chain, or the final sink. Note: you can only inspect the code under captures;

Example value pattern: ^sig_[a-z0-9]{4,8}-[a-z0-9]{4,8}-[a-z0-9]{6,10}$
Observable: {"type": "console", "action": "media.sign", "field": "req_sig", "pattern": "^sig_[a-z0-9]{4,8}-[a-z0-9]{4,8}-[a-z0-9]{6,10}$"}

